From: Zen Dodd <mail@steadytao.com>
Subject: syscall: skip unsupported symlink chmod

Backport of RsyncProject/rsync#1148, merged upstream after v3.5.2 as
ea645201fefbba7f6b6b22b621856dba3c01cdd3. Its test is left out.
https://github.com/RsyncProject/rsync/pull/1148

Linux answers fchmodat(AT_SYMLINK_NOFOLLOW) on a symlink with EOPNOTSUPP.
3.5.2 reports that as "failed to set permissions" and exits 23 whenever a
transfer with -E or -p creates a link.

diff --git a/syscall.c b/syscall.c
--- a/syscall.c
+++ b/syscall.c
@@ -1806,6 +1806,8 @@ int do_chmod(const char *path, mode_t mode)
 				code = 1;
 # elif defined AT_FDCWD && defined AT_SYMLINK_NOFOLLOW
 			code = fchmodat(AT_FDCWD, path, mode & CHMOD_BITS, AT_SYMLINK_NOFOLLOW);
+			if (code < 0 && (errno == ENOTSUP || errno == EOPNOTSUPP || errno == ENOSYS))
+				code = 1;
 # else
 			code = 1;
 # endif
